Every key clears BOTH bars -> CONVERGED, the intended outcome. No key fell short
of either target, so there is no shortfall section.

MARGIN THE HARDER TARGET ADDED: 10%. It moved OscFreq's window inward to
[3.42, 3.58], TuningRange to 660 MHz and OutputPower to 11 dBm. NOTE FOR THE
CALLER, because it is a real gap in the two-bar scheme: for a CEILING key the
harder bar is LOOSER than the real one (Power <= 3.3 vs <= 3.0 mW), so
"every harder key met" is NOT a superset of "every real key met". Both were
scored independently on every iteration for exactly this reason.

--- WHERE THE MARGIN IS THIN --------------------------------------------------
OscFreq sits 0.036 GHz (1.0%) below its upper bound and only 0.016 below the
harder upper bound -- the tightest number in the table. THIS IS DELIBERATE, NOT
DRIFT. Layout parasitics on the tank nodes can only ADD capacitance, and f0
falls as 1/sqrt(C), so f0 can only move DOWN from here. Sitting high in the
window is the whole available buffer: it gives 0.164 GHz (4.6% in f, i.e. ~9.5%
in C_node, roughly 48 fF per node) of room before the real 3.4 GHz floor is hit.
Centring at 3.5 GHz would have halved that buffer for no gain.

