--- NO FIGURE -----------------------------------------------------------------
generate_plot_script.py was NOT run. spec_analysis.log calls for no
response-shaped figure and there is none to draw: an oscillator has no frequency
response, and the plot generator is built around an .ac raw file this design does
not produce. The settled differential waveform is available as
sizing/simout_vco_lc_pre.out if a time-domain figure is wanted later.

--- NO OP-POINT DATA, ALL FIVE ITERATIONS -------------------------------------
Stated plainly rather than left to read as "nothing to see": generate_op_probe.py
is the only producer of per-device gm/gds/id/vds/vgs/vdsat/cgg, and it cannot
splice this deck (three independent failures, detailed in run_sizing_vco_lc.py's
docstring and in book_keeper.log's header). Every decision in the loop was made
from spec deltas plus the analytic tank model in spec_analysis.log. That model
was not taken on trust -- it reconciles with measurement (C_node = 856 fF
back-solved from the baseline f0 vs ~856 fF summed device-by-device) and it
predicted iter 1's frequency to 1.3% and iter 2's TuningRange to 8%.

--- WHAT A FURTHER RUN WOULD NEED ---------------------------------------------
NOTHING, for the spec as written. Every key clears both bars, the loop converged
in 3 real moves, and 10 of 15 iterations went unspent. DO NOT RE-INVOKE THIS
SKILL for this spec: more iterations cannot improve a converged result, and the
next thing that can change any of these numbers is a layout, not a width.

ONE DECISION IS LEFT WITH THE CALLER, and it is a genuine trade, measured rather
than argued (book_keeper.log ITER 3):

    netlist            Power       OutputPower   all REAL keys   all HARDER keys
    N4_M = 4 (SHIPPED) 2.73107 mW  12.6558 dBm   MET             MET
    N4_M = 3           2.18784 mW  10.3123 dBm   MET             MISS (OutputPower)

  M=3 is a 19.9% power saving that still meets the entire real spec. It was NOT
  shipped because it leaves 0.31 dB of OutputPower margin, and
  circuit_decomposition.yaml ranks the tank nodes `severity: high` with a
  mechanism that attacks exactly that key (layout C lowers f0, R_p falls as
  w0^2, amplitude falls with it). There is no netlist in between and no way to
  buy the amplitude back, both established by measurement rather than assumed:
  M is an integer count of parallel devices so 3 and 4 are adjacent; N5_W scales
  reference and leg together so it moves headroom, not the ratio; and the tank-Q
  lever is dead (iter 1 -> iter 2 changed OutputPower by -0.006 dB across a 50%
  varactor widening).
  If the user would rather have the 0.54 mW than the 2.3 dB, the change is a
  single `--set N4_M=3` re-run -- one iteration.

IF THE SPEC ITSELF CHANGED, the levers and their signs are known and measured:
  OscFreq up      -> XC0/XC1 w,l down   (also raises TuningRange and OutputPower)
  TuningRange up  -> XN2/XN3 w up, then XC0/XC1 w,l down to put f0 back
  OutputPower up  -> N4_M up (costs Power proportionally; the ONLY lever)
  Power down      -> N4_M down (costs OutputPower ~20*log10 of the ratio)
Two further things are fixed and would need a topology or model change, not
sizing: the coil (3.986 nH / 9.225 ohm, frozen) and Iref (300 uA, a TESTBENCH
source, not a device parameter).
